// affine_translate_mass.ri — CLI eval fixture: a MASS translation is rejected.
//
// affine_translate(5kg, 0kg, 0kg) returns Value::Undef (a translation is a
// DISPLACEMENT and must be LENGTH — task 5747, units-length ζ / R12), and the
// post-Undef geometry diagnose hook must emit on stderr:
//   error: affine_translate: dx/dy/dz argument expects Length, got Mass Scalar;
//          pass a dimensioned length such as `5mm`
// `reify eval` exits 1 — this is the genuine 0 -> 1 flip. Before ζ the same
// source exited 0 and printed
//   affine_map(linear=[[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]], translation=[5, 0, 0])
// i.e. the MASS dimension was silently discarded and 5 kg became 5 METRES.
//
// Lives in tests/fixtures/ (NOT examples/) since it intentionally triggers a
// runtime Error diagnostic.
//
// Declares its module explicitly: without it, `reify eval` also emits
// W_MODULE_DECL_MISSING ("expected `module affine_translate_mass`"), whose text
// contains the substring "affine_translate" and would independently supply an
// assertion needle for free — the trap task 6155 documented in
// affine_scale_dim.ri's own header.

module affine_translate_mass

structure def AffineTranslateMass {
    let m = affine_translate(5kg, 0kg, 0kg)
}
